Section 140 - Power of Magistrate to furnish written instructions, etc.-(1) Where the Magistrate directs a local investigation by any person under section 139, the Magistrate may- (a) furnish such person with such written instruction as may seem necessary for his guidance;
(b) declare by whom the whole or any part of the necessary expenses of the local investigation shall be paid.
